cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use DART in your research, please cite it as below."
title: "DART: Diffusion-Augmented Reliable Transformer Serving"
type: software
authors:
  - family-names: "Aydiner"
    given-names: "Tugrap"
repository-code: "https://github.com/tugrapaydiner/dart"
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-06-17"
keywords:
  - speculative decoding
  - diffusion language models
  - KV-cache compression
  - LLM inference
  - exact verification
abstract: >-
  DART is a single-sequence LLM inference engine that decouples throughput
  from fidelity: lossy draft lanes (block-diffusion canvases, multi-token
  prediction, n-gram retrieval, compressed- and sparse-KV self-drafting)
  propose token blocks that a full-precision target model verifies in one
  forward pass, so exact mode is byte-identical to the target's greedy
  decode by construction. Canvas reconciliation, a diffusion-specific
  recovery step, re-noises and repairs the unverified canvas suffix after a
  rejection instead of redrafting it.
